dns-provision: builds the configuration of the replicas of the internal DNS cluster.

  inventory            the replicas: name and address
  unbound.conf.tmpl    template of a replica's unbound.conf
  rebuild.conf         settings of the rebuild job

A replica is never edited by hand. It is rebuilt in place: the old instance is stopped, its directory is wiped,
a fresh configuration is rendered and a new instance is started and checked.

  sudo dns-rebuild ns1              rebuild replica ns1
  sudo dns-rebuild --dry-run ns1    print what a rebuild would render, touch nothing
  /opt/dns-provision/provision --help    options of the renderer

Rendered configurations: /etc/dns-cluster/<replica>/unbound.conf
Shared by all replicas:  /etc/dns-cluster/internal.zone.conf (internal names), /etc/dns-cluster/root.hints
Services:                dns-ns1 .. dns-ns4, logs in /var/log/dns-<replica>/
Log of the rebuilds:     /var/log/dns-rebuild/rebuild.log
